Done. Here's how the Python 3.10 switch actually works this time:

Why This Works vs. condacolab
condacolab installs a conda environment but Colab's kernel process continues pointing to the system Python — so the version never actually changed.
​

The deadsnakes approach works differently:

Installs Python 3.10 at the OS level via the deadsnakes PPA

Installs ipykernel for Python 3.10

Overwrites Colab's python3 kernel spec with python3.10 -m ipykernel install --user --name python3 — this replaces the kernel definition file that Colab reads on startup

After the auto-restart, Colab loads that kernel spec and the entire session — notebook cells, sys.executable, subprocess calls, pip, everything — runs under Python 3.10

Step 0b has a hard assert sys.version_info[:2] == (3, 10) so you'll know immediately if something went wrong before wasting time on any other steps.

